        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jack Sock, Raffaella Reggi, Liezel Huber, Bob Bryan, Melanie Oudin, Catarina Lindqvist, Claudia Kohde-Kilsch, Silke Meier\n- Organizations: Association of Tennis Professionals\n- Events: 2011 US Open – Mixed Doubles, Oslo Open\n- Roles: professional tennis players, defending champions, runner-up\n\nFacts:\n- Raffaella Reggi was born on 27 November 1965 and is a former professional tennis player from Italy.\n- Jack Sock was born on September 24, 1992 and is an American professional tennis player.\n- At the Oslo Open, Catarina Lindqvist won the singles competition, while Claudia Kohde-Kilsch and Silke Meier won the doubles.\n- At the Oslo Open, Raffaella Reggi finished runner-up in both singles and doubles.\n- At the 2011 US Open – Mixed Doubles, defending champions Liezel Huber and Bob Bryan lost in the second round to teenage compatriots Melanie Oudin and Jack Sock.\n- Jack Sock was ranked world No. 21 in men's singles by the Association of Tennis Professionals.",
